From b183fb8bae7802b7ccb61ccae5131b6356eba645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:44:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/79] demux: ps: carry the whole track across a PSM version
 change

When a program stream map announces a new version, each track is rebuilt
into a stack ps_track_t and assigned over the live one. Only fmt is
initialised there, and ps_track_fill() sets just i_skip, i_id and fmt, so
b_seen, i_next_block_flags, i_first_pts and i_last_pts are indeterminate
when the structure is copied. es is replaced on the next line; those four
are not.

DEMUX_GET_TIME subtracts i_first_pts from the current timestamp, and
DEMUX_SET_TIME uses it to build the ratio it forwards to
DEMUX_SET_POSITION, so a seek lands anywhere. The track is the same
elementary stream either way, so carry those fields over.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h b/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h
index 623fdb90da..655604d7e4 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h
+++ b/modules/demux/mpeg/ps.h
@@ -736,6 +736,16 @@ static inline int ps_psm_fill( ps_psm_t *p_psm, block_t *p_pkt,
         es_format_Clean( &tk[i].fmt );
 
         tk_tmp.b_configured = true;
+        /* Carry the rest of the track over. This is the same elementary
+         * stream, only its format has changed, and ps_track_fill() only
+         * fills in i_skip, i_id and fmt. Without this the assignment below
+         * copies indeterminate values into the live track, which
+         * DEMUX_GET_TIME and DEMUX_SET_TIME go on to read. es is the one
+         * exception, being replaced on the line after the copy. */
+        tk_tmp.b_seen = tk[i].b_seen;
+        tk_tmp.i_next_block_flags = tk[i].i_next_block_flags;
+        tk_tmp.i_first_pts = tk[i].i_first_pts;
+        tk_tmp.i_last_pts = tk[i].i_last_pts;
         tk[i] = tk_tmp;
         tk[i].es = es_out_Add( out, &tk[i].fmt );
     }
